From: Llaminar native event lifetime regression
Subject: [PATCH] Borrow the exact live producer generation for event capture checks

HIP events remain valid after their producer stream is destroyed. Capture
checks previously dereferenced the unowned stream pointer, producing a host
use-after-free, mutex abort or hang during retained tensor-event retirement.
Address-only membership also mistakes a reused stream address for the original
producer. Use the existing device stream registry and monotonic stream ID to
borrow the exact generation for capture metadata inspection. No queue owner,
allocation, device transfer, synchronization or graph scheduling mode is added.

Pinned base: ROCm/rocm-systems 6b0e43f341195e203754e08f850e437ff2fc09f9
             (therock-10.0, ROCm Core SDK 10.0.0)

diff --git a/hipamd/src/hip_internal.hpp b/hipamd/src/hip_internal.hpp
--- a/hipamd/src/hip_internal.hpp
+++ b/hipamd/src/hip_internal.hpp
@@ -597,6 +597,36 @@
     void RemoveStream(Stream* stream);
     /// Returns true if stream belongs to this device
     bool StreamExists(const Stream* stream);
+
+    /**
+     * @brief Borrow one registered stream generation without retaining its queue.
+     * The reader lock prevents RemoveStream from retiring the object until the
+     * inspection ends. The monotonic identity rejects a new stream allocated at
+     * a retired producer's address. A missing producer is a valid event state:
+     * the recorded amd::Event owns its completion independently of the stream.
+     */
+    class StreamLease final {
+     public:
+      StreamLease() = default;
+      StreamLease(const StreamLease&) = delete;
+      StreamLease& operator=(const StreamLease&) = delete;
+      StreamLease(StreamLease&&) = default;
+      StreamLease& operator=(StreamLease&&) = default;
+      /// Return the live producer only for this lease's lexical lifetime.
+      Stream* get() const { return stream_; }
+     private:
+      friend class Device;
+      StreamLease(Device& device, Stream* stream, uint64_t identity)
+          : lock_(device.streamSetLock_),
+            stream_(device.streamSet_.count(stream) != 0 &&
+                    stream->GetStreamId() == identity ? stream : nullptr) {}
+      std::shared_lock<std::shared_mutex> lock_;
+      Stream* stream_ = nullptr;
+    };
+    /** @brief Authenticate and borrow an event's original producer generation. */
+    StreamLease BorrowStream(Stream* stream, uint64_t identity) {
+      return StreamLease(*this, stream, identity);
+    }
     /// Synchronize all streams (optionally only blocking ones)
     void SyncAllStreams(bool cpu_wait = true, bool wait_blocking_streams_only = false);
     /// Returns true if any stream on this device is in capture mode
